      "dh_downy_note": "Bill about a third of the head — short and stubby, like a tack.",
      "dh_hairy": "Hairy Woodpecker",
      "dh_hairy_note": "Bill as long as the head is wide, or longer — a chisel.",
      "dh_note": "The plumage is near enough identical, so size alone will not settle it at distance. The red bar under each bill is its length; the blue bar under each head is the head width. Compare those two, not the whole bird.",
      "dh_title": "Downy or Hairy? Measure the bill against the head",
