      "foil_alt": "Cross-section of a wing. The upper surface is curved and the lower is nearly flat. Air splitting at the front travels further over the top than underneath, and an arrow marks lift pointing upward.",
      "foil_fast": "longer path over the top",
      "foil_lift": "lift",
      "foil_note": "Curvature is drawn larger than life so it is visible — a real wing is far subtler. Flatter sections (falcons, auks) trade lift for speed; deeper ones (hawks, vultures) lift more at low speed.",
      "foil_slow": "shorter path underneath",
      "foil_title": "Cut through the wing — this curve is the lift",
