      "why_universal_free_meals_matter": "Why universal free meals matter: ",
      "wic_programs_community_health_centers_": "WIC programs, community health centers, public housing nutrition education, SNAP-Ed. Direct patient education + community programming.",
      "winter_fisheries_food_deserts": "Winter, fisheries, food deserts",
      "withdrawing_from_social_activities_tha": "Withdrawing from social activities that involve food (lunch, parties, family meals)",
      "without_it": "Without it",
      "working_with_eating_disorders_requires": "Working with eating disorders requires emotional sustainability",
      "you_decoded_this_label_correctly_move_": "You decoded this label correctly. Move to the next challenge.",
      "you_don_t_have_to_wait_for_things_to_g": "You don't have to wait for things to get worse to ask for help. You don't have to \"earn\" support by being sick enough. You just have to reach out.",
      "you_don_t_need_to_know_what_to_say_the": "You don't need to know what to say. They're trained to start the conversation. You can call back. You can hang up. You can't do it wrong.",
      "you_don_t_owe_anyone_your_attention_re": "You don't owe anyone your attention. Removing harmful accounts is a self-care move, not rudeness.",
      "you_or_someone_you_love_can_come_throu": "You — or someone you love — can come through this.",
      "your_body_has_three_different_ways_to_": "Your body has three different ways to make ATP. They're all running constantly, but the dominant system depends on how hard and how long you're working.",
      "your_body_holds_only_50_g_of_atp_at_an": "Your body holds only ~50 g of ATP at any moment, but recycles it constantly: each ATP molecule cycles ATP → ADP → ATP about 1,000+ times per day. Total ATP turnover roughly equals your body weight per day. The recycling happens in tiny organelles called mitochondria, which use oxygen and food (glucose, fatty acids) to charge ADP back into ATP.",
      "your_body_needs_at_least_your_bmr_wort": "Your body needs at least your BMR worth of energy to keep its essential systems working. Eating well below BMR for an extended time forces the body to slow metabolism, break down muscle, weaken immunity, and impair concentration. The goal isn't to \"minimize calories\" — it's to give your body what it needs to do its job. If anything in this module triggers worry about how much you're eating, please talk with a trusted adult, your doctor, or NEDA (1-800-931-2237).",
      "your_day_in_numbers": "Your day, in numbers",
      "your_hypothesis_which_macro_most_affec": "Your hypothesis (which macro most affects satiety? Glycemic load? They're different.)",
      "your_plate_is_empty_add_foods_above_to": "Your plate is empty. Add foods above to begin.",
      "your_school_counselor_or_school_psycho": "Your school counselor or school psychologist ",
      "bm_back_to_plate": "Back to the Macronutrient Lab",
      "bm_candidate_note": "These are candidates, not a diagnosis. Symptoms have many causes; a doctor can test for a nutrient shortfall.",
      "bm_card_desc": "Pick any nutrient and watch the organs that use it glow on a glass 3D figure, with a stream tracing the route from your gut. Click an organ to see everything it depends on. Then predict before you look: which region is iron's main address?",
      "bm_card_subtitle": "3D — where each nutrient goes to work",
      "bm_card_title": "Nutrient Body Map",
      "bm_clear_region": "Clear region selection",
      "bm_compare_footnote": "Sharing an address does not make two nutrients interchangeable — they do different jobs once they arrive. Overlap tells you where a shortfall of either would be felt.",
      "bm_compare_legend": "On the figure these burn brightest; a region only one of them serves sits dim.",
      "bm_compare_none": "None",
      "bm_compare_only": "only",
      "bm_compare_only_2": "only",
      "bm_compare_second": "Compare",
      "bm_compare_shared": "Shared addresses",
      "bm_compare_title": "Two nutrients, one body",
      "bm_compare_why": "Why this pair is worth knowing",
      "bm_compare_with": "with",
      "bm_controls": "3D view controls",
      "bm_desc_line": "Glowing organs use the selected nutrient; dots trace the route from the gut. Drag or use the buttons to turn the figure. Click an organ to select it.",
      "bm_energy_copy": "This is your body doing nothing at all: lying still, awake, not digesting a meal. Most of the fuel you eat is spent here, not on exercise. The bigger an organ glows on the figure, the larger its share.",
      "bm_energy_headline": "The number worth remembering",
      "bm_energy_headline_copy": "Your brain is about 2% of your body weight and spends about 20% of your resting energy — and a teenage brain, still building connections, spends a larger share than an adult one. Thinking is expensive, and it is paid for out of what you eat.",
      "bm_energy_open_module": "Open Energy & Metabolism",
      "bm_energy_other": "🫧 Everything else",
      "bm_energy_other_note": "Skin, gut, immune cells, bone, blood and fat tissue. Individually small, together a fifth of the bill.",
      "bm_energy_source": "Healthy-adult averages from Wang et al. (2010) and Brody, Nutritional Biochemistry. Real shares vary with body composition, age and health — these describe the pattern, not a person.",
      "bm_energy_title": "Where your resting energy goes",
      "bm_explored": "explored",
