      "manuscript_ink_was_water_based_and_bea": "Manuscript ink was water-based and beaded off metal type. Gutenberg adapted oil-painting varnish into a printer’s ink that clung to the type face, transferred cleanly to paper, and dried without bleeding. The recipe is short. Getting it right took years.",
