      "the_100_year_reference_system_that_die": "The 100+ year reference system that died. Dewey + Library of Congress classification. Why catalog cards mattered.",
      "the_1450_press_was_wood_and_your_two_a": "The 1450 press was wood and your two arms. The 2026 desktop printer is plastic, electronics, and a USB cable. Both put ink on paper. The shape of the work moved off your back and into a kilowatt.",
      "the_1450_type_case_was_organized_by_fr": "The 1450 type case was organized by frequency: the most-used letters (E, T, A, O, I, N) sat in the easiest compartments to reach. When the Linotype arrived in 1886, designers had a fresh chance to lay out a keyboard from scratch. They did not pick alphabetical. They picked frequency.",
      "the_21st_century_letterpress_revival_h": "The 21st-century letterpress revival. Hatch Show Print (Nashville since 1879). Wedding invitations + art prints + craft brewery labels. Letterpress is alive.",
      "the_32_page_format": "The 32-page format",
      "the_95_theses": "The 95 Theses",
      "the_aztec_mexica_empire_maintained_ext": "The Aztec (Mexica) empire maintained extensive book traditions: tribute records, historical chronicles, religious texts, divinatory almanacs, land deeds. After conquest, some traditions continued under Spanish supervision — the Florentine Codex (1545-1590), compiled by Franciscan friar Bernardino de Sahagún with Nahua scholars, is a 12-volume ethnographic encyclopedia in Nahuatl + Spanish. It is the most extensive surviving documentation of pre-conquest Mesoamerican civilization. Sahagún's collaborators (named in the text) deserve as much credit as he does.",
      "the_bay_psalm_book": "The Bay Psalm Book",
      "the_bold_lurid_covers_that_defined_pul": "The bold lurid covers that defined pulp era. Frank R. Paul, Margaret Brundage, Virgil Finlay. A serious illustration tradition.",
      "the_book_as_object": "The Book As Object",
      "the_british_library_has_the_entire_gut": "The British Library has the entire Gutenberg Bible online as a high-resolution facsimile. Spend 15 minutes scrolling. Try to read a line of Blackletter. Notice what you can and cannot decode.",
      "the_cast_type_would_work_for_limited_r": "The cast type would work for limited runs but the workshop would lose money to recasting and lost impressions.",
